From 778b0ee1ea20b2ce20e79f21d65ea69dc47ebe18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <remora@localhost>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 19:46:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] res: load the LineageOS platform resource APK into every
 process

The LineageOS SDK ships two halves and only one of them was reachable.
Platform apps (Settings, LineageParts) static-link org.lineageos.platform
.internal, so the Lineage classes and their generated R class compile in
fine -- and that R class points at package id 0x3f, which lives in a
separate APK, org.lineageos.platform-res.apk, built with
--allow-reserved-package-id --package-id 63. Nothing put that APK on any
app's asset path, so every 0x3f lookup threw:

  Resources$NotFoundException: String array resource ID #0x3f020004
    at lineageos.hardware.LineageHardwareManager.<init>:204
    at lineageos.preference.ConstraintsHelper.checkConstraints:180
    at lineageos.preference.ConstraintsHelper.<init>:74
    at lineageos.preference.SelfRemovingPreference.<init>:24
    at com.android.settings.DisplaySettings.onCreate:68

i.e. Settings > Display died on inflate, and so would the other six
screens carrying one of the 13 lineageos.preference widgets.

This is NOT the <library>/uses-library mechanism: there is no
<library name="org.lineageos.platform"> anywhere in the tree and no app
declares uses-library, because a shared-library entry would only add the
jar to the classpath. The resources have to come from the zygote's shared
system asset set, next to framework-res.apk -- which also explains why
lineage_sdk_common.mk allow-lists the SDK into /system rather than
/system_ext ("AOSP has no support of loading framework resources from
/system_ext"): the path is hardcoded here.

Deleting the offending preferences was the alternative and it does not
work. ConstraintsHelper's constructor calls checkConstraints
unconditionally, so removing one widget just moves the crash to the next
one in the XML.

With the resources resolvable the constraint machinery does its job
instead of throwing: requiresFeature="lineagehardware:*" routes to
LineageHardwareManager.isSupported(), the AIDL/HWC2 lookups both come up
empty on a container with no Lineage HAL, and the widget tombstones
itself. No LineageSystemServer is required for that -- getService()
returning null is handled, and the resulting Log.wtf is non-fatal with
wtf_is_fatal unset.

TWO FILES, AND THE SECOND ONE IS NOT OPTIONAL. Loading the APK in the
zygote leaves its fd open across every fork, and zygote enforces a static
allowlist of inheritable fds. Without the fd_utils.cpp entry the first
fork aborts and the device NEVER BOOTS:

  JNI FatalError called: (system_server) Not allowlisted (64):
      /system/framework/org.lineageos.platform-res.apk
  init.svc.zygote: restarting   (system_server processes: 0)

Learned by deploying the AssetManager half alone and boot-looping the
instance. framework-res.apk sits in that same list one line up for
exactly the same reason.

Best-effort by design on the load itself. The enclosing catch turns any
IOException into "Failed to create system AssetManager", i.e. a boot
loop, so a tree that ships no lineage-sdk (or a Ravenwood host run) must
not reach it.

Change-Id: I0f27caa0234a292efd609ef9d2a602551b4979b8
---
 .../java/android/content/res/AssetManager.java | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 core/jni/fd_utils.cpp                          |  3 +++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/java/android/content/res/AssetManager.java b/core/java/android/content/res/AssetManager.java
index e18ba2238905..56a9b58b892b 100644
--- a/core/java/android/content/res/AssetManager.java
+++ b/core/java/android/content/res/AssetManager.java
@@ -84,6 +84,10 @@ public final class AssetManager implements AutoCloseable {
     public static final String FRAMEWORK_APK_PATH = getFrameworkApkPath();
     private static final String FRAMEWORK_APK_PATH_DEVICE = "/system/framework/framework-res.apk";
     private static final String FRAMEWORK_APK_PATH_RAVENWOOD = "ravenwood-data/framework-res.apk";
+    // Not under /system_ext: nothing resolves a framework resource APK from there, which is why
+    // vendor/lineage/config/lineage_sdk_common.mk allow-lists the SDK into /system.
+    private static final String LINEAGE_RES_APK_PATH =
+            "/system/framework/org.lineageos.platform-res.apk";
 
     private static final Object sSync = new Object();
 
@@ -284,6 +288,20 @@ public final class AssetManager implements AutoCloseable {
             final ArrayList<ApkAssets> apkAssets = new ArrayList<>();
             apkAssets.add(ApkAssets.loadFromPath(frameworkPath, ApkAssets.PROPERTY_SYSTEM));
 
+            // The LineageOS platform resources (reserved package id 0x3f). Platform apps
+            // static-link org.lineageos.platform.internal, whose generated R class points at 0x3f,
+            // but nothing else ever puts the resource APK on their asset path — so every such
+            // lookup throws Resources$NotFoundException. Loading it here, in the zygote's shared
+            // system set, is what makes @*lineageos.platform:* resolvable process-wide.
+            // Best-effort on purpose: a tree that ships no lineage-sdk must not lose zygote, and
+            // the enclosing catch turns any IOException into a boot loop.
+            try {
+                apkAssets.add(
+                        ApkAssets.loadFromPath(LINEAGE_RES_APK_PATH, ApkAssets.PROPERTY_SYSTEM));
+            } catch (IOException e) {
+                Log.w(TAG, "Not loading " + LINEAGE_RES_APK_PATH + ": " + e.getMessage());
+            }
+
             // TODO(Ravenwood): overlay support?
             final String[] systemIdmapPaths =
                     RavenwoodHelperBridge.getInstance().isRunningOnRavenwood() ? new String[0] :
diff --git a/core/jni/fd_utils.cpp b/core/jni/fd_utils.cpp
index bf6ff81c9294..a41ec788f7ca 100644
--- a/core/jni/fd_utils.cpp
+++ b/core/jni/fd_utils.cpp
@@ -44,6 +44,9 @@ static const char* kPathAllowlist[] = {
         "/sys/kernel/debug/tracing/trace_marker",
         "/sys/kernel/tracing/trace_marker",
         "/system/framework/framework-res.apk",
+        // Loaded beside framework-res.apk in the zygote's system asset set, so its fd is inherited
+        // across every fork and has to be allowlisted for exactly the same reason.
+        "/system/framework/org.lineageos.platform-res.apk",
         "/dev/urandom",
         "/dev/dri/renderD129", // Fixes b/31172436
         "/dev/stune/foreground/tasks",
-- 
2.54.0

